          "path": "_m/d/n/5/b/underground-atlanta-wp/1917-maxwell-one-ton-express-d.jpg",
          "filename": "1917 Maxwell One Ton Express (Description) (Underground Atlanta).JPG",
          "caption": "1917 Maxwell\nMaxwell Motor Company\nTarrytown, New York\nFounded in 1905\nA Maxwell One Ton Express was featured in the standard catalogue of American light duty truck for that year.\nIt is powered by a four-cylinder engine and is started by use of a hand crank.  Note the 1920’s Moto Meter on the radiator.  This device was added to show the water temperature.\nBegun as Maxwell-Brisco, the Maxwell Motor Company eventually became part of Chrysler.\n\n\nLocation: Underground Atlanta, Old Alabama St., SW, Atlanta, GA, USA",
          "alt": "1917 Maxwell\nMaxwell Motor Company\nTarrytown, New York\nFounded in 1905\nA Maxwell One Ton Express was featured in the standard catalogue of American light duty truck for that year.\nIt is powered by a four-cylinder engine and is started by use of a hand crank.  Note the 1920’s Moto Meter on the radiator.  This device was added to show the water temperature.\nBegun as Maxwell-Brisco, the Maxwell Motor Company eventually became part of Chrysler.\n\n\nLocation: Underground Atlanta, Old Alabama St., SW, Atlanta, GA, USA",
          "width": 2048,
